      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Closing a bean whose work has already landed (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Paid twice in one session, on `r1lz` and again while sweeping for others.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "`r1lz`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Closing a bean whose work has already landed (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "`xd1s`'s note said \"seven workflows\" and named six; four files actually carry the group, and the invariant holds by *group **or** retry*, which is what its gate asserts. `lx2s`'s is *\"Issue #215 can be closed by its author\"*, and an agent never closes an issue on its own say-so.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "`xd1s`",
        "`lx2s`",
        "#215"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reconciling closes in bulk — and an owner's reopen outranks your evidence",
      "prov:value": "It adds one of its own, because a store can carry an **owner's reopen sweep**: the owner moved beans from `completed` back to `todo` or `in-progress` because the earlier close was not good enough. **Measured in `qou` 2026-10-04 (bean `yr93`).** The owner's 2026-09-08 sweep (`qou-7sin`, commit `a61496d`, *\"reopen 18 beans whose own body says they are open\"*) had reopened beans that still carried a `close(<id>)` commit on main. Four of those (`7vm4`, `8xb1`, `ftuv`, `s2gm`) would have been re-closed by any reconciler that matched closing commits to status, on the very evidence the owner had rejected.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `yr93`",
        "`7vm4`",
        "`8xb1`",
        "`ftuv`",
        "`s2gm`",
        "owner's",
        "owner",
        "2026-10-04",
        "2026-09-08"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-08",
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-33",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Re-derive from the REMOTE, never from your checkout (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**Two occurrences in one session, 2026-09-21, bean `pomp`.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `pomp`",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-34",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Re-derive from the REMOTE, never from your checkout (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "When the claim is *\"nobody has built this\"*, check the open branches too; this session started building `ankg`, `s8nu` and a `viewer-prune` module that siblings had already landed or had in flight, **five times**, and the check that would have prevented each is one `git diff --name-only origin/main...<branch>`. Tool: a path, a prefix or a bean id, against `main` and every open PR head (bean `pomp`, reopened 2026-10-24 after the f1e1 duplicate in [`bean-drain`](bean-drain.md) §\"The measured case\").",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "`ankg`",
        "`s8nu`",
        "bean `pomp`",
        "2026-10-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-35",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "When you cannot re-derive it yourself — `ready-to-close`",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-09-20, bean `bbbl`.** Four beans read as finished in their own bodies and sat `in-progress`: `7uff` (*\"Everything on this bean is now done … Ready to resolve once the owner confirms; not resolving unilaterally\"*, 0 of 7 boxes ticked), `t0i3` (its one open box done in the body at commit `8d1c8f27`), `y8as` (both halves merged, the platform copy sha256-verified and deleted), `d1r6` (a full `## Implemented` section, 0 of 5 ticked).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean `bbbl`",
        "`7uff`",
        "`t0i3`",
        "`y8as`",
        "`d1r6`",
        "owner",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-36",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When you cannot re-derive it yourself — `ready-to-close`",
      "prov:value": "The measurement may need a running deployment, a branch this container does not have, or a judgement the owner reserved.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-coordination.md#provenance-37",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where a sibling session is visible from (STRICT)",
